"""Provisional reusable framework boundary proven inside SalixTorrent.

Names and package structure remain internal working contracts until the wider
RAD/framework extraction is complete. Modules under this namespace must stay
independent of SalixTorrent views, BitTorrent logic, localization content and
concrete desktop backend adapters.

Intra-framework imports are package-relative so this directory can be copied
and renamed as one unit during extraction experiments. Backend-neutral
responsive coordination consumes an injected host contract; native resize
hooks remain in application/backend adapters. Backend-neutral rolling telemetry
and realtime plot coordination follow the same rule: data/model contracts live
here while concrete plotting remains adapter-owned. Keyed live-table and
categorical state-grid models likewise keep identity/change semantics here while
concrete widgets/canvases remain presentation-host responsibilities. Explicit data-view, selection, ordered-item, command-state and command-menu coordination add interaction semantics without GUI callbacks or reactive machinery. Mixed-layout placement is likewise parent-local: automatic containers can reserve the occupied bounds of explicitly offset children while concrete positioning remains renderer-owned. Provisional designer metadata can describe proven component types, properties, hierarchy relationships and geometry as JSON-safe snapshots without constructing toolkit objects or freezing a final project schema. A separate snapshot-editing layer applies explicit property commands with deterministic undo/redo history, while structural designer commands add validated insert/remove/reorder/reparent operations and child-slot metadata on the same immutable snapshots. Optional document-level copy/paste/duplicate tooling captures immutable subtrees, remaps node IDs deterministically and feeds the same structural validation/history boundary without introducing an operating-system clipboard or final project schema. Stable-ID designer selection/focus state remains ephemeral and separate from document history while surviving accepted edits and preview replacement. Backend-neutral hierarchy navigation can traverse parent/child/sibling/preorder relationships and compute stable reveal paths, while a separate hierarchy projection model derives visible rows and owns ephemeral expanded IDs without giving toolkit tree widgets authority over designer state. A backend-neutral property-inspector projection now derives deterministic selected-node rows and semantic editor hints from the existing DesignerPropertyState metadata without owning selection or bypassing validated edit/history contracts. A backend-neutral designer-workspace coordinator composes project/dirty/history, hierarchy, selection, inspector and preview state into one shell-facing snapshot while delegating every mutation to those existing owners. A backend-neutral editor-shell command model projects stable File/Edit/Navigate command trees and dynamic availability from that workspace while leaving file-dialog, new-project template and paste-placement policy to the shell. A post-v0.5.1 designer-shell menu presenter now binds that semantic command tree to the existing renderer-neutral command-menu host contract, refreshing state before presentation and revalidating dispatch without importing a concrete toolkit. A concrete designer hierarchy-panel presenter now binds current `DesignerHierarchyRow` projections to an injected host while delegating selection/focus and expansion back through `DesignerWorkspace`; Dear PyGui/Tkinter tree items remain disposable adapter state rather than semantic owners. A concrete designer property-inspector presenter now binds the existing selected-node inspector projection to injected editor hosts; toolkit controls remain disposable views while validation, undo/redo, dirty state and preview replacement continue through the existing workspace/edit-session owners. A clickable designer preview-selection presenter now exposes the current rendered preview as stable-ID click targets through injected hosts; native hit-testing and transient selection outlines remain adapter-owned while selection/focus/reveal stay in the workspace. A catalog-backed designer component-palette presenter now projects reusable component metadata through injected hosts and emits explicit placement requests instead of fabricating nodes or guessing parent/slot/relationship policy. A backend-neutral component-placement resolver now consumes those requests, projects explicit parent/slot/index/relationship choices, carries missing self-describing type metadata into the same checked structural transaction, and creates sparse visible nodes only after confirmation; concrete hosts remain form adapters rather than insertion-policy owners. Selected-node Move Up/Move Down/Remove commands now project through the same semantic shell, while a renderer-neutral shortcut bridge maps normalized keyboard gestures onto those existing command keys; native key registrations remain adapter-owned and never become document policy. A provisional designer-project file boundary can now own one edit session, wrap its immutable snapshot in a strict versioned JSON envelope, and atomically save/load that document without persisting selection, hierarchy expansion, clipboard, history, callbacks or runtime services. A first preview bridge can reconstruct supported snapshot types into a new backend-neutral Component tree while preserving designer IDs, and an optional preview host can replace those reconstructed trees transactionally from checked edit/undo/redo/copy-paste operations. Rendered designer previews now layer human-scale generic control defaults over the active renderer profile without persisting those defaults into documents; explicit width/height values still win and remain editable through the inspector. A backend-neutral preview-resize coordinator now commits one completed selected-component pointer gesture through the same checked width/height transaction while concrete hosts own transient handles, hit-testing and drag feedback. A shared numeric-drag translator now gives Inspector scrubbing and preview resizing one normal/Shift/Ctrl sensitivity contract, while Inspector reset groups all current Default-capable properties into one checked composite edit; toolkit hosts own only transient pointer feedback. Linear rows/columns now make cross-axis sizing explicit: natural child geometry is the default and stretch is an opt-in parent policy rather than an accidental widest-sibling effect. A conservative hierarchy drag planner resolves stable source/target IDs only into unambiguous metadata-free reparent operations and delegates the edit through the existing workspace/structural history owner; toolkit tree hosts never choose relationship semantics. This tooling remains additive: code-first applications may compose the same Component/runtime contracts directly and never import designer modules. Callbacks, application bindings, specialized semantic-field factories and incremental live synchronization remain later work. That portability is an internal boundary guarantee only; it does not freeze a final package name, version, or public API.
"""
